pve-ups-panel (2.1.0) stable; urgency=low

  * Add 69-pve-ups-panel.rules: vendor-level USB UPS udev catch-all rules
    for CyberPower, APC, Eaton, Tripp Lite, Powercom, Belkin, Phoenixtec.
    Complements NUT's product-specific rules (62-nut-usbups.rules) to cover
    new or unrecognised models. MODE=0660 GROUP=nut.
  * postinst/prerm: reload udev rules and re-trigger USB subsystem on
    install and removal.

 -- YoMin Su <aaaa1234567891016@gmail.com>  Thu, 29 May 2026 01:00:00 +0800

pve-ups-panel (2.0.0) stable; urgency=low

  * Complete rewrite: multi-tab architecture replacing single-panel design.
  * Phase 1: PVE.ups.View card layout, EmptyState, 7-tab scaffold,
    DeviceSelector toolbar, monkey-patch injection into PVE.node.Config.
  * Phase 2-3: Overview page with SetupWizard (3-step), live dashboard
    connected to GET /nodes/{node}/ups API.
  * Phase 4: Backend PVE::API2::UPS multi-module (Config, Scan, RRD,
    Battery, Shutdown, Notify, Log), NUT ups.conf CRUD, USB scan.
  * Phase 5: Device Management page — DeviceEditWindow, service status,
    start/stop/restart controls.
  * Phase 6: History page — 4 proxmoxRRDChart charts, RRD.pm backend
    with rrdtool create/update, pve-ups-panel-rrdcollect timer.
  * Phase 7: Battery Health page — health card, quick/full test with
    confirm dialogs, polling, test history grid.
  * Phase 8: Shutdown Rules page — global/recovery hbox, VM/CT grid,
    ShutdownRuleEditWindow, Shutdown.pm with qm/pct integration.
  * Phase 9: Notifications page — PVE endpoint list, 8-event rules grid,
    NotifyEditWindow (TagField), Notify.pm, pve-ups-notify NUT hook,
    Handlebars email templates.
  * Phase 10: Logs page — event log grid (newest first), Clear button
    (Sys.Modify), Log.pm backend.
  * Phase 11: i18n complete — 212 strings translated into 31 languages
    (zh_TW, zh_CN, de, fr, es, it, pt_BR, ru, ja, ko, pl, nl, tr, cs,
    sv, da, nb, nn, hu, hr, sl, bg, ukr, ca, eu, fa, gl, he, ar, ka).
  * Packaging: dpkg-divert for Nodes.pm and index.html.tpl, systemd
    timer for RRD collection, full prerm/postinst lifecycle.

